# MCP Odoo — invariants (example)

⚠️ Never mutate (`update_record` / `delete_record` / `post_message`) a `record_id` that was not READ in THIS session — if you must mutate by id, put a dedicated provenance gate in front of it.
Check whether a `payment.token` is really stored before assuming an automatic charge: a subscription can be invoiced on the Odoo side without being collected automatically, depending on the integration.
A due date generated in advance can look inconsistent (a due date earlier than the issue date). That is a known generation quirk of some subscription modules, not a customer payment refusal.
`list_models` returns Odoo's generic catalogue (200+ models), not the models your instance actually uses — narrow it with a targeted `search_records` rather than walking the whole list.
